ch we can deploy and view  okay so now we've opened this dashboard  we can see here this is really  uh quite a nicely laid out dashboard we  get our sidebar  which we can collapse everything is  responsive  and we see our trips here we see  our geographic plots here so once again  we could kind of  select some subset of the data again i'm  going to select here  on the airport  and see what that selection looks like  uh now we can see the distributions here  in history rooms here update to reflect  that selection  and so that's quickly gives us an idea  of  how uh trips here in the at the airport  uh differ from trips otherwise right  and so we can for example see the trip  distances are much longer from the  airport which makes a lot of sense  uh we can again see the distribution  here change quite a bit  and so on so we could further narrow  that down and say really  uh well i'm only interested in really  low fares  so four to six dollars where did people  go  from the airport on ford from two to six  dollars  and so again make sense uh only very  short distances show up now  um very short distances here  um i think i kind of broke the selection  so we're going to reset  this what you probably can't see here is  also that we get a little  progress indicator but i'm probably  currently just hovering over my own  image  so that's fine um so  yeah just within a few lines of code we  generated this really quite complex  dashboard  um from our  the components that we defined in our  notebook  all right uh at this point i really need  to thank  the organizers of this conference um i'm  sure it's  i'm very excited for various talks i  also need to thank john neese who  implemented  the first version of link selections and  i'm really looking forward to your  questions in the  q a sessions thanks very much  i hope you learned a lot and  please try out our tools thanks very  much


